From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 01:14:04 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8132-j604: Add the keyboard alias

The loaders find the internal keyboard through /aliases/keyboard, as on
the other Apple laptops (t8112-j413.dts, t8132-j713.dts):

- U-Boot (arch/arm/mach-apple/board.c j713_prepare_input) requires it to
  publish the MTP input handoff, and rtkit_helper.c uses it to disable the
  DockChannel HID node together with &mtp when it cannot keep the session.
- m1n1 (kboot.c) uses it to set the keyboard layout and HID country code
  from the Apple device tree.

Without it U-Boot disables &mtp but leaves &mtp_hid enabled, and there is
no keyboard before Linux. The alias joins serial0 from t8132-jxxx.dtsi.

The boot framebuffer keeps its power domains (disp_fe and dptx_phy). The
J713 deletes them because its board power-domain policy disables
dptx_phy and hands disp_fe to the firmware; the J604 has no such policy,
so without the framebuffer as a consumer genpd would power dptx_phy off
at boot while the firmware framebuffer is still being scanned out.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts
index 196ab80e28..189c141064 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604.dts
@@ -21,6 +21,10 @@
 	compatible = "apple,j604", "apple,t8132", "apple,arm-platform"; /* DTV-ROOT-1 */
 	model = "Apple MacBook Pro (14-inch, M4, 2024)";
 
+	aliases {
+		keyboard = &keyboard;
+	};
+
 	led-controller {
 		compatible = "pwm-leds";
 		led-0 {
